instructions:
We consider the standard sentence-level relation extraction setting, where we are given a sentence in which two entities are highlighted, which we refer to as the head entity and tail entity. The goal is to predict which relationship holds between these two entities, given a pre-defined set of candidate relation labels. The relation labels are Freebase relations (/domain/type/property): the head entity is the subject and the tail entity is the value. Choose NA if none of the listed relations holds from the head entity to the tail entity.

Sentence (head entity marked <e1>...</e1>, tail entity marked <e2>...</e2>): {marked_sentence}
Head entity: {head}
Tail entity: {tail}
